{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787270008273555001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"spongy-illjudged-terrier","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f29c03c314c19f59cb58c6a6fdbeeb6e8dd5ffc2a9d35bebe68744e232c854cb","event_uuid":"048fbc5c-6893-4066-8c31-1ed633bf12c7","position":{"commit_sha":"2991a7fd5bbde0e6f4afe443e0e22faa9d30e321","position":"1787267960390491001-048fbc5c-6893-4066-8c31-1ed633bf12c7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5924e455f2e954bdf7fdb9e33144d3b0df134a639b1ae034ebad79b13fe7f8af","event_uuid":"fa6aa236-bd02-494c-a9fd-4788905baeb0","position":{"commit_sha":"f5006f88f90559d346aeb25d988adde2eb5b9f02","position":"1787267970382342001-fa6aa236-bd02-494c-a9fd-4788905baeb0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787267960390491001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fa6aa236-bd02-494c-a9fd-4788905baeb0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3198-438c-72a5-470f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`llm.enrich.enrich()` builds its prompt from a ticket's full material with **no bound on the\nresulting size**. For the largest tickets in this store that prompt now exceeds the model's\ncontext window outright, so every enrichment attempt fails at the provider:\n\n```\npydantic_ai.exceptions.ModelHTTPError: status_code: 400,\n  model_name: us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0,\n  'Message': 'The model returned the following errors:\n              prompt is too long: 206826 tokens > 200000 maximum'\n  -> rebar.llm.errors.LLMUnavailableError\n```\n\n`enrich_drain.drain` catches that per item and leaves the claim to lease-expire\n(\"will retry after lease\"), which is the right posture for a TRANSIENT provider failure. But\nthis failure is deterministic and size-driven: the retry cannot succeed, and the ticket only\ngrows. The entry therefore cycles forever — claimed -> lease expires -> pending -> claimed —\nand is never marked done.\n\n## Evidence (2026-08-20, this repo's own store)\n\nThree entries, enqueued **2026-08-14**, still undone six days later:\n\n```\n8625-7bea-67db-4cdc   9305-b42c-3262-4c58   e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2\n```\n\nThese are the three largest ticket directories in the store (870 / 747 / 621 event files) —\nthe most re-certified tickets, so both the most often re-enqueued and the largest prompts.\nObserved two full cycles within twenty minutes (claims at 16:02 by `drainer-41817-1`, again at\n16:17 by `drainer-63784-1`, neither reaching `done`), and confirmed the cause by calling\n`enrich()` directly on `e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2`: it fails in 2.8 s with the 400 above.\n\nNothing is logged where an operator would look. The failure is reported via\n`logger.warning(..., exc_info=True)` inside the drain child, whose stderr goes to\n`.rebar/logs/enrich-drain.log` — but the drain child that hits it is spawned from an ordinary\nwrite, and the log has not recorded these failures at all, so the wedge is invisible.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis is the SECOND of two independent causes keeping this store's enrichment queue non-empty.\nThe first — a detached drain child inheriting a removed worktree's cwd and dying at\n`getcwd()` — is bug `3198-438c-72a5-470f`, fixed separately. With that fixed, drain children\nsurvive and claim, but these three entries still never complete, so the queue is never quiet,\n`958e-f4b3-275c-4154`'s O(1) gate marker fast path stays unreachable on this store, and the\n`enrich drain gate check took ~Nms` warning keeps firing on ordinary writes. Both causes have\nto be fixed before that acceptance criterion is observable here.\n\n## Scope (to be confirmed by whoever claims this)\n- `src/rebar/llm/enrich.py` — bound the prompt (truncate/summarise/sample the ticket material\n  against the model's context window before the call).\n- `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py` — distinguish a PERMANENT per-item failure from a transient\n  one so a deterministic failure is not retried forever in silence (a poison-pill /\n  attempt-count posture, and an operator-visible signal).\n- Consider whether `rebar doctor` should surface a queue entry that has been re-claimed N\n  times without completing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A ticket whose material exceeds the model context window enriches successfully (bounded\n      prompt) rather than raising a 400.\n- [ ] A deterministically-failing entry stops cycling silently: it is either completed or\n      marked in a way an operator can see, rather than re-claimed forever.\n- [ ] The three entries above reach `done` on this store.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and CI's pytest invocation are green.\n\n## Provenance\nFound while fixing `3198-438c-72a5-470f` (conscious-weighable-spittlebug). That bug's fix was\nverified to work — a detached drain child now survives its spawning worktree's removal — and\nthis is what remained: the surviving child claims these entries and still cannot finish them.\nDifferent file, different mechanism, so filed rather than folded in.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"569c-931f-69a2-4c1d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"enrichment prompt is unbounded, so the largest tickets can never drain","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["048fbc5c-6893-4066-8c31-1ed633bf12c7","fa6aa236-bd02-494c-a9fd-4788905baeb0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787270008273555001,"uuid":"de11194e-3aa4-4276-a25b-9d7cb271cfcf"}